  "step_3": "The decision reason is inapplicable because no outcome in either lottery has a probability below 20%—the 20% outcome in Lottery B is not below 20%, so no adjustment is triggered. Therefore, the reason cannot be applied to this decision problem. Furthermore, the individual’s justification focuses solely on the 80% probability of 4,000 Euros and does not consider the low-probability outcome or any adjustment of probabilities. Since the reason is not applicable and the individual did not consider or use any such adjustment, there is no evidence that the reason was used. The individual’s reasoning is based on a straightforward comparison of a high probability of a higher payoff versus a certain lower payoff, not on a modified weighting of small-probability outcomes. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
